<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <title>Noah Humbert</title>
        {% include 'partials/_head.html.twig' %}
    </head>
    <body>
        <!-- Top Navitation Bar-->
        {% include 'partials/_navbar.html.twig' %}

        <!-- Top Banner -->
        <div class="container mt-2 mb-5 text-center">
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-12">
                    <p class="fs-1 my-0">Noah Humbert</p>
                    <p class="fs-5 my-0">I build software and electronics that actually work</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row mt-3 justify-content-center">
                <div class="col-lg-2 col-6 d-grid gap-2">
                    <a class="btn btn-primary" href=" {{ path('business-card') }} ">Contact Me</a>
                </div>
                <div class="col-lg-2 col-6 d-grid gap-2">
                    <a class="btn btn-secondary" href=" {{ path('projects') }} ">Projects</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- About Me Portion -->
        <div class="container my-5">
            <div class="row justify-content-center mb-2">
                <div class="col-11">
                    <div class="card" style="max-width: auto;">
                        <div class="row g-0">
                            <div class="col-md-4">
                                <img src=" {{ asset('images/noah.jpg') }} " class="card-img-top" alt="Noah">
                            </div>
                            <div class="col-md-8">
                                <div class="card-body">
                                    <h5 class="fs-2 mb-4">About me</h5>
                                    <p class="fs-6 mb-0">
                                        I have loved technology since I can remember. I started in elementary school building games on a website called Scratch. That love
                                        of creating transitioned into simple websites and into an even stronger love for IT. I started an IT support position at 16 years
                                        old and haven't looked back since. I have developed not only more software engineering skills and computer knowledge, but also
                                        lifelong friends and connections. This role has also helped me achieve a deep understanding of IT operations and infrastructure
                                        from an enterprise business standpoint. Instead of going down the traditional college path, I decided to stay in this role while building my skills every single day with 
                                        hands-on experience. Building, breaking, fixing, and improving electronics, software, and business processes has become an
                                        extremely enjoyable hobby for me.
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Featured Project -->
        <div class="container mt-5">
            <div class="row">
                <p class="fs-1 text-center">Featured Project</p>
            </div>
            <div class="row justify-content-center mb-2">
                <div class="col-12 col-lg-10">
                    <div class="card" style="max-width: auto;">
                        <div class="row g-0">
                            <div class="col-md-4">
                                <img src=" {{ asset('images/logo.png') }} " class="card-img-top resume-experience" alt="OFS Logo" style="margin-top: 15%;">
                            </div>
                            <div class="col-md-8">
                                <div class="card-body">
                                    <p class="fs-4">Breadboard Computer</p>
                                    <p class="fs-5">
                                        I just started this one! This is my journey to building an 8-bit computer that is Turing Complete on breadboards with just
                                        IC chips. No microcontrollers allowed. Watch the full journey from an explaination of transistors all the way to creating our
                                        own assembly language for the CPU. This series will be filmed in it's entirety on YouTube!
                                    </p>
                                    <a class="btn btn-primary" href=" {{ path('my-website') }} ">Learn More</a>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="container my-5">
            <div class="row">
                <p class="fs-1 text-center">Contact Me</p>
            </div>
            <div class="row justify-content-center">
                <div class="col-12 text-center">
                    {% include 'partials/_business-card.html.twig' %}
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Javascript -->
        <script src="{{ asset('bootstrap/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js') }}"></script>
    </body>
</html>